<p>Nepali guide Kami Rita Sherpa summited Mount Everest on Sunday for the 32nd time, extending his own record for the most ascents of the world’s highest mountain, Nepal’s Department of Tourism said. The 56-year-old reached the 8,849-metre peak at 10:12 a.m. while guiding clients for 14 Peaks Expedition, according to the department and expedition accounts. Another Nepali climber, Lhakpa Sherpa, 52, also climbed Everest on Sunday, extending her women’s record to 11 summits, officials and expedition sources said. Nepal’s tourism authorities congratulated Kami Rita for what they called a historic milestone and cited his contribution to mountain tourism.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/FM6U-CIYaJhEtPVeDrCUKneFLjrG5n19R_QVqcqez3E8jZCsJwYFpHvOf9U4m30m6okIZ6fJtUEWSaiW_IWKm3blSsoDoR1onmUaGdSc1HohOlGyzLAhoogv' alt='Nepali guide Kami Rita Sherpa, who climbed Mount Everest for the 32nd time' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Climbing season: Nepal issued a record 492 Everest climbing permits for the 2026 spring season, with about 1,000 climbers expected on the mountain when guides are included.</li><li>Safety toll: At least three Nepali climbers have died on Everest this month during the March-to-May climbing season, according to reports citing Nepalese authorities.</li><li>Other records: Among non-Sherpa climbers, British guide Kenton Cool has 19 Everest summits, while Americans Dave Hahn and Garrett Madison have 15 each.</li><li>Crowding factors: Expedition companies cited restrictions on the Tibetan side of Everest and difficult weather and ice conditions as factors that narrowed the safe climbing window this season.</li></ul><blockquote>Today, Nepali climbers have once again written history on this glorious mountain - Balen Shah</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Nepal Prime Minister Balen Shah: Shah said the achievements reflected unwavering courage, strict self-discipline and dedication to work. (<a href='https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/05/17/news/world/nepali-duo-break-own-records-on-everest/2345720'>The Manila Times</a>)</li><li>Nepal Tourism Department spokesperson Himal Gautam: Gautam told AFP the records could energize other climbers and said record-setting through healthy competition could help make climbing safer, more dignified and better managed. (<a href='https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/05/17/news/world/nepali-duo-break-own-records-on-everest/2345720'>The Manila Times</a>)</li><li>Seven Summit Treks: The expedition company said Kami Rita and his team were descending toward base camp after the summit and that preparations were underway in Kathmandu for a welcome. (<a href='https://english.onlinekhabar.com/kami-rita-summits-everest-32nd-time.html'>OnlineKhabar English</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/2000926/nepali-sherpa-scales-mount-everest-for-a-record-32nd-time'>Nepali Sherpa scales Mount Everest for a record 32nd time</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/nepals-mountaineer-kami-rita-sherpa-climbs-mt-everest-for-32nd-time-beats-own-record/article70989806.ece'>Nepal’s mountaineer Kami Rita Sherpa climbs Mt. Everest for 32nd time, beats own record</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/nepals-kami-rita-sherpa-climbs-mount-everest-for-32nd-time-breaking-his-own-record-11507282#publisher=newsstand'>Nepal&#x27;s Kami Rita Climbs Mount Everest For 32nd Time, Breaking His Own Record</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/17/two-nepali-sherpa-climbers-break-own-records-on-mount-everest'>Two Nepali Sherpa climbers break own records on Mount Everest</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/two-nepali-climbers-break-own-everest-records/a-77186761'>Two Nepali climbers break own Everest records</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://minutemirror.com.pk/everest-legend-breaks-record-again-557193/'>Everest legend breaks record again</a> - minutemirror.com.pk</li><